# motion-graphics — reference pack

This skill provides the **design vocabulary and motion reference** the main agent and scene builders use when authoring a motion-graphic scene. It does not dispatch subagents or create `videos/<project-name>`.

## How to use

1. The main agent chooses **one blueprint** from `skill://hyperframes-motion/blueprints/` and (optionally) **one rule** from `skill://hyperframes-motion/rules/`.
2. The blueprint's category is resolved through `skill://hyperframes-motion/catalog.json`.
3. Scene context includes the resolved category reference and relevant grounding material.

## Skill references

- **Catalog map**: `skill://motion-graphics/catalog-map.md`
- **Categories**: `skill://motion-graphics/categories/`
- **Grounding**: `skill://motion-graphics/grounding/`
- **Builder contract**: `skill://motion-graphics/references/builder-contract.md`
- **Motion vocabulary**: `skill://motion-graphics/references/motion-vocabulary.md`
- **Samples**: `skill://motion-graphics/samples/`
